### Register: expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":" Kai2@Example.com ","password":"password123","displayName":" Kai "}

### Duplicate: expect 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"test@example.com","password":"password123","displayName":"Kai"}

### Invalid fields: expect 400 with an errors map
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"not-an-email","password":"short","displayName":""}

### JWT Resource
GET http://localhost:8080/api/anything

### Login: expect 200 with a token (saved for later requests)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":" KAI2@example.com ","password":"password123"}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### Wrong password: expect 401
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"kai2@example.com","password":"wrong-password"}

### Unknown email: expect the same 401 body
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"nobody@example.com","password":"password123"}

### Me with token: expect 200 with the Kai2 user
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Me without token: expect 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me